# Wave W17-Y (Vernal Path): bloom elm — a lane elm in soft greens carrying its own blossom: a broad crown flecked pink and white where the bloom sits in the leaf, highlight lifted clear of the turf, on bloom turf (ground baked in). The Vernal Path’s own tree — split from Route 214’s verge pine beside it by form entire (flowering broadleaf vs meadow conifer) and from Lake Gallant’s shore elm by the blossom: that elm shades a lake road, this one is part of the banks.
